pes requires all three suits and winds and dragons. I have winds (F2), but no dragons yet. Possible but not immediate.\n\nGiven the tile availability: T6 has 1 left unseen; T8 has 1 left; T2 has 2; T4 has 2; etc. B2 has 4 left, so my pair is safe. W6 has 4 left, but it's not useful currently.\n\nI think the best discard is W6 because it's an isolated tile from a different suit, and removing it simplifies my hand towards possibly a Half Flush or All Types. Keeping T5 and T7 offers more chow possibilities in Bamboo, and keeping B2 as pair is essential.\n\nReason: I must retain the B2 pair as it is my only pair. Discarding W6 removes a lone tile from a third suit, potentially moving toward a hand concentrated in two suits or aiming for All Types. T5 and T7 can combine with T6 to form a chow, and T6 is still available (1 left). This gives me a better chance to complete a meld quickly. Discarding T5 or T7 would reduce my connectivity in Bamboo.\n\nAnswer: Play W6"}
